<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian Nationalist Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tautininkai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian Nationalist Union (Tautininkai) was a nationalist political party founded in 1924, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanas-smetona">Antanas Smetona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustinas-voldemaras">Augustinas Voldemaras</a>. After the military coup of December 1926 it became the ruling party of Smetona's authoritarian regime and from the mid-1930s the only legal party. It was dissolved after the Soviet occupation in 1940.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-nationalist-union.jpg" alt="Lithuanian Nationalist Union" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KrustyToast4 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_Lithuanian_Nationalist_Union.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Smetona dissolved the Seimas in 1927, sidelined his more radical prime minister Augustinas Voldemaras in 1929 and ruled until 1940 as an authoritarian president supported by the <b>Lithuanian Nationalist Union</b>, with new constitutions in 1928 and 1938 strengthening his position.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania">Republic of Lithuania · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
